The title says it all:  I would like to publicly denounce the notion that
a shield or amulet of reflection is necessary to win NetHack 3.1.  Yes, it IS a
very handy thing to have, but it is not an absolute necessity.

My current character is 22nd level, on Dungeon level 37, and going down.  He 
hasn't been below 80% of maximum hit points in a long time, and has never 
had any reflection item...simply because I had better things to use those 
_eight_ wishes on, and I haven't found any reflection item in the dungeon.

Okay, quick question.  How many of you think that I am totally-out-of-my-
skull crazy for doing this?  :)  A lot, I'll bet.  Seriously, though, here
is why I haven't bothered to get reflection:

I don't need it.  I just don't.  With permanent invisibility and AC -24, I
simply don't get hit by wands or breath attacks, and I have the following 
resistances anyway:
  
	magic resistance
	poison resistance
	sleep resistance
	fire resistance
	cold resistance
	shock resistance
	disintegration resistance

Simply put, any attack that reflection would stop wouldn't do me damage anyway.
Mind you, I got all those wishes (except the first) after I got all those nice
intrinsics.  If I had gotten another wish early, I probably _would_ have taken
a shield of reflection then...

Comments or opinions, anyone?

